### Phase 4A Session 3 smoke tests
### Run end-to-end against a fresh `npm run dev` server.
### Compatible with the VSCode "REST Client" extension and JetBrains HTTP client.
###
### Usage:
###   1. Start the server: `cd server && npm run dev`
###   2. Click "Send Request" above each block top-to-bottom.
###   3. The {{token}} variable is set automatically from the register/login response.

@host = http://localhost:3001
@username = smoke_{{$timestamp}}
@password = correcthorsebatterystaple

### Health check
GET {{host}}/api/health

### Register a fresh user — saves token into {{token}}
# @name register
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "{{username}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

@token = {{register.response.body.token}}

### Who am I?
GET {{host}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Settings: should be {} for a fresh account
GET {{host}}/api/settings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Settings: auto-sync write
PUT {{host}}/api/settings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "settings_json": {
    "playerSpawnRate": 1.5,
    "avlColors": { "available": "#0a0" },
    "unitTypeColors": {}
  }
}

### Settings: read back
GET {{host}}/api/settings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### List private worlds (empty at first)
GET {{host}}/api/private-worlds
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create a private world
# @name createWorld
POST {{host}}/api/private-worlds
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Smoke Test World"
}

@worldId = {{createWorld.response.body.id}}

### List private worlds (should show one)
GET {{host}}/api/private-worlds
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### List saves for the world (empty)
GET {{host}}/api/private-worlds/{{worldId}}/saves
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Save a slot
POST {{host}}/api/private-worlds/{{worldId}}/saves
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "slot_name": "slot1",
  "state_json": {
    "money": 250000,
    "stations": [],
    "gameDay": 1,
    "gameSeconds": 0
  }
}

### Overwrite the same slot (should upsert, not duplicate)
POST {{host}}/api/private-worlds/{{worldId}}/saves
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "slot_name": "slot1",
  "state_json": {
    "money": 300000,
    "stations": [],
    "gameDay": 2,
    "gameSeconds": 60
  }
}

### List saves (should still be one slot, updated saved_at)
GET {{host}}/api/private-worlds/{{worldId}}/saves
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Read the slot back
GET {{host}}/api/private-worlds/{{worldId}}/saves/slot1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Ownership test: another user cannot read my world
# @name register2
POST {{host}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "smoke2_{{$timestamp}}",
  "password": "correcthorsebatterystaple"
}

@token2 = {{register2.response.body.token}}

### Should return 404 (not 403, to avoid leaking world existence)
GET {{host}}/api/private-worlds/{{worldId}}/saves
Authorization: Bearer {{token2}}

### Delete the slot
DELETE {{host}}/api/private-worlds/{{worldId}}/saves/slot1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Delete the world
DELETE {{host}}/api/private-worlds/{{worldId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Verify world is gone
GET {{host}}/api/private-worlds
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
